WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.369
Joe: From exclusive
items to portion sizes,

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:04.004
we wanted to find all the differences

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:06.906
between KFC in the US and Italy.

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.708
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:12.078
New season, Italy. New host.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:13.847
I want to introduce you to a familiar

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:16.016
Food Insider face: Claudia.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:20.220
Let's start with the
Original Recipe chicken.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.188
If you're buying just
the original chicken,

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:25.392
you can get a two-piece. One is huge.

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:27.327
We also have lots of bucket options,

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:30.030
but most of them combine
the Original Recipe,

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.531
wings, and tenders.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:33.299
If you only want the original chicken,

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:36.302
the largest size we have
is a six-piece bucket.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.937
Looks a bit scary.

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:40.707
The other bucket options
include a variety of chicken,

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:43.043
such as tenders and hot wings.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:45.145
For example, if you
want to feed two people,

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:47.080
you can get the 10-piece bucket.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:51.217
This contains four tenders
and six crispy tenders.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:53.119
And if you want to feed four people,

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.788
you can get this big boy here.

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:56.756
This one is a 16-piece bucket

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:59.426
and contains four Original Recipe,

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:03.163
four tenders, four crispy
tenders, and four wings.

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:05.832
This is actually the
biggest thing on the menu.

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:08.968
Then in the US, KFC's chicken
comes in four portion sizes.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.971
You can start off by getting
a one-piece à la carte,

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.973
then a two-piece with a combo,

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.475
a three-piece with a combo,

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:17.777
and a four-piece with a combo,

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.612
all of which come with
a side of your choice,

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.114
a biscuit, and a drink.

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:25.218
Then for the buckets,
we have an eight-piece,

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:27.087
the 12-piece,

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.726
and last but not least,
this luscious bucket,

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.929
16 pieces of chicken.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:38.264
Dinner is served in America.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:41.134
You can get those in
either original or crispy.

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.735
That makes our biggest bucket

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:46.473
166% bigger than Italy's.

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:49.275
I've actually never really had KFC before.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.077
Chicken is not so popular in Italy,

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:54.013
especially fried chicken served like that.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:56.483
So I'm really curious to try it and see.

00:01:58.985 --> 00:01:59.986
Yeah, nice.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:02.956
Not a lot of spices. It's
just, like, fried chicken,

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:06.192
which is what we were promised.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:08.895
Let's see how one chicken drumstick weighs

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:09.796
compared to Italy.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.564
Claudia: 64 grams.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:12.999
Joe: 97 grams.

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:16.302
Is anyone surprised that the
chicken in the United States

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:18.872
is bigger than every other country

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.573
we've done this "Food Wars" with?

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.475
In Italy, we also have hot wings,

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:25.011
and they come in a five-piece

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:27.747
and in a 18-piece bucket.

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:30.216
This one is designed for three people.

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:32.519
18 wings in the US is definitely

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:34.220
for one person, not three.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:37.490
I could have six wings
and then have a full meal.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.926
So, they're advertised as hot wings.

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:44.164
I think to an Italian palate,

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:46.633
yeah, you could say these are spicy.

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:48.168
We also got wings here in the US.

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:51.938
Now, currently, at least the
KFC I went to here in Burbank

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:55.675
has one size of wings, the eight-piece.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:56.943
Go ahead and take the bones out.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:02:59.712
Crispy.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.581
Heat I can notice that isn't overwhelming.

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:02.582
Perfectly fine.

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.883
Next are the fries.

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.785
In Italy, you can get three sizes:

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:08.054
a small, medium, and large.

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:11.157
In the US we got two sizes of fries:

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:13.893
the individual and the large.

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:15.762
Claudia: Let's weigh our biggest size.

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:18.598
[laughs] I never grow tired of that.

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:20.600
Is this the lowest we've gotten?

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:21.968
We've gone to the same KFC every time,

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.937
but apparently they
have fired that scooper

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:26.172
because he or she was being too generous.

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:29.375
In Italy, KFC offers drinks in two sizes:

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:30.944
a medium and a large.

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:34.514
Drinks in the US, you get
two fountain-drink sizes,

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:36.449
the regular and the large.

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:38.685
I will point out to you,
Claudia, and the rest of Italy,

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:42.522
that our regular, the smallest
drink you can get at a KFC,

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:44.958
is 591 milliliters,

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:48.828
which is much bigger than your large.

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:51.998
But if you really want
your thirst quenched,

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:56.169
you can get yourself the big boy. Guszh!

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:58.838
That is a half gallon, 64 fluid ounces,

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:03.443
or 1,892.7 milliliters

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:04.477
of beverage.

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:07.180
Claudia: Let's measure the
large one to see if that's true.

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:09.382
Joe: Supposed to be 887.

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:11.351
Let me just see if we can
get it up to 800. Whoa.

00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:12.852
This is just 800.

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:15.655
The messes that this
show forces me to make.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:21.160
If you are incredible at balancing
and you don't want a cap,

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.128
I guess this is OK

00:04:22.128 --> 00:04:25.732
if you're just going to sit
at your table like [slurps].

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:30.236
Here's everything that you
can get at KFC in Italy

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:32.105
that you won't find in the US.

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:34.407
Here's everything you'll
find at a KFC in the US

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:36.109
you won't find in Italy.

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:40.146
We have one exclusive chicken
option you can't get in Italy.

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:42.248
That is the extra-crispy.

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:43.683
This is probably close to what you get,

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:44.784
the Original Recipe.

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:46.085
And then you got the extra-crispy.

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:48.054
I mean, obviously, it's night and day.

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:49.255
Volume up on this one.

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:52.659
This is regular [crunching],

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:57.096
and of course the extra-crispy
[louder crunching].

00:04:58.665 --> 00:05:00.700
If you're wondering, yes, way better,

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.535
way more flavorful. Mm!

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:05.338
We don't have extra-crispy
chicken here in Italy,

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:07.173
but if you order tenders,

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:10.176
you're going to get original and crispy.

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:12.045
It does look much crispier.

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:16.549
It also looks, it just
looks much sadder as well,

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:18.551
because it's literally flopping.

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:20.553
At least I can see the chicken.

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:22.288
I can see some meat in there.

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:25.525
This one is completely
hidden in the batter.

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:27.026
Like, it could be anything.

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:31.097
Another exclusive are the KFC nuggets.

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:33.266
You can get these in
varieties of five, eight,

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:35.535
12, and 36.

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:36.936
I went with the five-piece.

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:39.539
Now, Claudia, take a good look at this.

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:41.808
You in Italy have popcorn chicken.

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:44.210
Besides potential size differences,

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:46.512
I really don't know what else
is different about these.

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:48.381
In Italy we don't have nuggets,

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:50.950
but we have popcorn chicken.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:54.687
We got the large, but it comes
also in small and medium.

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:56.322
Quietly sometime last year,

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:58.958
KFC just took popcorn
chicken off the menu,

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:00.259
and I'm pretty bummed about that.

00:06:00.259 --> 00:06:02.729
I mean, I like the nuggets,
but the popcorn chicken, man.

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:04.397
It's just something because
they're a lot smaller,

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:06.232
and then the chicken-to-skin ratio

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:07.900
is more in favor of the skin,

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.669
so you get a lot of that
savory skin in there.

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:10.703
RIP, popcorn chicken.

00:06:10.703 --> 00:06:13.039
You're very lucky, Claudia.
You are very lucky.

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:15.475
Were you guys the guinea pigs for this,

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:19.312
or are we the guinea pigs for
a new recipe or something?

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:22.682
I think I prefer a whole piece.

00:06:22.682 --> 00:06:25.752
I think bingeing on
little bits of chicken,

00:06:25.752 --> 00:06:28.054
it's so un-Italian

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:31.257
that I'm not sure that I'll
be getting used to that.

00:06:31.257 --> 00:06:34.527
Snacking on little bits of fried chicken

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:36.462
while in a convenient to-go box

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:37.930
while driving or walking around

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.799
is so American, and I love it.

00:06:39.799 --> 00:06:41.601
I gotta try these.

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:43.102
This is what America's all about.

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:45.671
Let's move on to the chicken sandwiches.

00:06:45.671 --> 00:06:48.508
In Italy, we have the Zinger.

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:52.912
This is supposed to be Italy's
version of the spicy chicken

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:54.380
that you guys have in the US.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:57.083
I don't know, Joe, how does
that look like? Similar?

00:06:57.083 --> 00:06:59.218
Yes, Claudia, your Zinger sandwich

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:02.789
looks a little bit like
our spicy chicken sandwich.

00:07:02.789 --> 00:07:05.057
Here's ours, and we only
have pickles on ours,

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:06.459
so no lettuce and tomato.

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:09.328
But after I took a bite,

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:11.764
you can see there's, like, some red here,

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:13.466
so that's supposed to be the spice.

00:07:13.466 --> 00:07:16.736
There's the tiniest, tiniest,
tiniest spice, to be honest.

00:07:16.736 --> 00:07:19.939
Then, moving on, we have
this tiny little thing,

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:21.040
the Krunky.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:22.608
Crunchy or Krunky.

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:24.377
This one here is on the value menu,

00:07:24.377 --> 00:07:27.213
so it's a cheaper option.

00:07:27.213 --> 00:07:30.950
And then we've got the Colonel,
named after Colonel Sanders.

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:33.219
We don't really have colonels here.

00:07:33.219 --> 00:07:35.922
I think we do, but we
keep them for the army.

00:07:35.922 --> 00:07:37.957
I don't think they've ever
opened a chicken restaurant.

00:07:37.957 --> 00:07:39.859
Then we got the Double Colonel.

00:07:39.859 --> 00:07:42.695
Does that mean that another person joined?

00:07:42.695 --> 00:07:46.299
Then we have the Kentucky
chicken and bacon.

00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:47.967
I have to say, this is the biggest bacon

00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:50.903
that I've seen in
Italian fast-food chains.

00:07:50.903 --> 00:07:53.439
This to me feels quite, quite fake.

00:07:53.439 --> 00:07:55.741
You can also get this one in a double.

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:58.277
And then we have the chicken grilled.

00:07:58.277 --> 00:08:01.881
So much sauce. Sad, sad
lettuce hanging off mayo.

00:08:01.881 --> 00:08:03.850
You can also get the double crispy,

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:07.353
which is two chicken tenders in a bun.

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:08.821
Here are sandwiches you can get in the US

00:08:08.821 --> 00:08:10.623
you can't get in Italy,
starting down here.

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:12.225
The classic Chicken Little.

00:08:12.225 --> 00:08:15.194
I don't know, it's just a
tender in between two buns.

00:08:15.194 --> 00:08:16.696
Here's what I would do: I would go to KFC,

00:08:16.696 --> 00:08:19.966
I'd stand in line, I'd order
my meal and get one of these,

00:08:19.966 --> 00:08:21.801
and then demand they give me this

00:08:21.801 --> 00:08:23.803
while I wait for the rest of my food.

00:08:23.803 --> 00:08:24.971
It's nothing. It's nothing.

00:08:24.971 --> 00:08:26.038
It's like an appetizer.

00:08:26.038 --> 00:08:29.308
And then, of course, just
the regular chicken sandwich.

00:08:29.308 --> 00:08:31.077
I have said on record several times

00:08:31.077 --> 00:08:34.013
that I think KFC might have the best

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:36.382
fast-food chicken sandwich in America.

00:08:36.382 --> 00:08:37.383
There's also apparently an

00:08:37.383 --> 00:08:39.519
ultimate barbecue fried chicken sandwich.

00:08:39.519 --> 00:08:41.454
That was new. I think it came and went.

00:08:41.454 --> 00:08:45.324
As an Italian, I'm not so
big on chicken burgers.

00:08:45.324 --> 00:08:47.660
I think the idea of
having chicken in a burger

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:50.830
doesn't really resonate so well with us.

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.732
So it almost hurts my eyes.

00:08:52.732 --> 00:08:54.667
There's just too much brown in it.

00:08:54.667 --> 00:08:57.036
Like, I want to see more color.

00:08:57.036 --> 00:08:59.772
Yeah, that's absolutely not the case here.

00:08:59.772 --> 00:09:02.208
As you can see, our chicken is deep-fried

00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:04.944
and covered in a mayo-y sauce.

00:09:04.944 --> 00:09:07.780
We're eating chicken
all the time in America.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:08.614
Yeah, we eat a lot of beef,

00:09:08.614 --> 00:09:10.283
but we also eat a lot of chicken,

00:09:10.283 --> 00:09:13.686
and it is in no way diet
food here. Not at all.

00:09:13.686 --> 00:09:17.223
We also used to have twisted
wraps here at KFC in Italy,

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:19.659
but suddenly they're
not on the menu anymore.

00:09:19.659 --> 00:09:21.093
They're still worth mentioning, though,

00:09:21.093 --> 00:09:24.397
because of the hilarious
advertising campaign.

00:09:24.397 --> 00:09:26.399
When KFC launched them in Italy,

00:09:26.399 --> 00:09:29.235
they actually designed
Italian leather handbags

00:09:29.235 --> 00:09:31.904
supposed to hold your Twisters,

00:09:31.904 --> 00:09:35.107
which is a bit of a knockoff
to the Fendi Baguette bag.

00:09:35.107 --> 00:09:37.410
All right, we might not have
Italian bags for our wraps,

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:39.879
but we do have KFC Crocs.

00:09:39.879 --> 00:09:41.147
Look how cool those look.

00:09:41.147 --> 00:09:41.981
[crickets]

00:09:41.981 --> 00:09:43.449
We do have a couple wrap options.

00:09:43.449 --> 00:09:45.952
You can only get them
through the KFC application,

00:09:45.952 --> 00:09:47.219
which is not how I ordered.

00:09:47.219 --> 00:09:49.355
Anyway, you can get the classic
one with a crispy tender.

00:09:49.355 --> 00:09:52.558
There's also a spicy one
that I assume is spicier.

00:09:52.558 --> 00:09:54.393
And, apparently, you can
get two of them for $5,

00:09:54.393 --> 00:09:57.930
which is a pretty good
deal. But I didn't get that.

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:00.700
Here's a few hilarious things
you can't get in Italy.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:02.268
Over here's the Famous Bowl.

00:10:02.268 --> 00:10:04.170
Yes, Claudia, I know you're
dying to know all about this,

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:05.404
so I will tell you now.

00:10:05.404 --> 00:10:09.642
It is nuggets, mashed
potatoes, gravy, corn,

00:10:09.642 --> 00:10:12.778
cheese, all in one convenient tub.

00:10:12.778 --> 00:10:15.381
So, this would be, I guess,
what's considered a bite.

00:10:16.582 --> 00:10:17.817
It's really heavy.

00:10:17.817 --> 00:10:20.953
It's gotta be 90% mashed potato.

00:10:20.953 --> 00:10:21.787
It's a lot.

00:10:21.787 --> 00:10:25.825
Another American exclusive
is this, a chicken pot pie.

00:10:25.825 --> 00:10:27.727
Look at the size of this thing.

00:10:27.727 --> 00:10:32.431
I think this would just
profoundly confuse every Italian.

00:10:32.431 --> 00:10:34.600
Here's the thing about the
mashed potatoes and gravy.

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.202
You have to get them together.

00:10:36.202 --> 00:10:38.804
Having them separately
seems very strange to me.

00:10:38.804 --> 00:10:41.607
It is a classic US side dish,

00:10:41.607 --> 00:10:43.776
especially with things like fried chicken.

00:10:43.776 --> 00:10:46.479
Apparently when Colonel
Sanders sold the business,

00:10:46.479 --> 00:10:48.914
he compared the mashed
potatoes in a Manhattan store

00:10:48.914 --> 00:10:51.784
to "wallpaper paste" topped with "sludge."

00:10:51.784 --> 00:10:53.052
But that was back in the '70s,

00:10:53.052 --> 00:10:54.920
so hopefully they've
made some improvements.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.455
I'd say that they have.

00:10:56.455 --> 00:10:59.725
I mean, I know, like, those
mashed potatoes look so dry.

00:10:59.725 --> 00:11:03.229
I understand you want to put
some sort of liquid on them.

00:11:03.229 --> 00:11:04.897
I'd just not have any of it.

00:11:04.897 --> 00:11:05.731
But for once,

00:11:05.731 --> 00:11:08.634
the potatoes don't look
radioactively yellow,

00:11:08.634 --> 00:11:10.736
so that should be a good sign.

00:11:10.736 --> 00:11:15.007
We happen to have some Italian-style
sides here on the menu,

00:11:15.007 --> 00:11:17.476
although I have no idea who
called this Italian style,

00:11:17.476 --> 00:11:19.945
because none of these
really look Italian to me.

00:11:19.945 --> 00:11:21.447
We have cheese puffs.

00:11:21.447 --> 00:11:24.483
To me, these look like fried Babybels.

00:11:24.483 --> 00:11:26.552
That's the only cheese that I can think of

00:11:26.552 --> 00:11:28.120
that has this shape.

00:11:29.555 --> 00:11:32.158
I think it's some kind of mozzarella.

00:11:32.158 --> 00:11:33.459
Yeah, OK.

00:11:33.459 --> 00:11:34.727
Yeah, we have bread.

00:11:34.727 --> 00:11:37.863
Just, like funny bread.

00:11:37.863 --> 00:11:39.932
It looks very dry, just by looking at it.

00:11:39.932 --> 00:11:43.035
And then we have corn on the cob.

00:11:43.035 --> 00:11:45.271
The US has off the cob.

00:11:45.271 --> 00:11:47.673
This is not Italian.

00:11:47.673 --> 00:11:50.443
I've never seen an Italian
person having corn on the cob.

00:11:50.443 --> 00:11:52.645
In Italy, we also have four salads,

00:11:52.645 --> 00:11:54.880
but we were not able to get them today.

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:56.649
Those are grilled chicken,

00:11:56.649 --> 00:11:58.984
crispy chicken, and original chicken,

00:11:58.984 --> 00:12:01.987
which, we don't know how that
differs from the crispy one,

00:12:01.987 --> 00:12:04.557
and a veggie salad.

00:12:04.557 --> 00:12:06.625
Right, Claudia, look at that.

00:12:06.625 --> 00:12:07.727
Look at that mac and cheese.

00:12:07.727 --> 00:12:08.994
It's American mac and cheese.

00:12:08.994 --> 00:12:12.631
I mean, I don't really have
thoughts about mac and cheese,

00:12:12.631 --> 00:12:15.367
because to me that's just not Italian.

00:12:15.367 --> 00:12:17.203
We just sort of gave up on it and be like,

00:12:17.203 --> 00:12:19.105
"You want it? It's yours."

00:12:19.171 --> 00:12:21.807
Yeah, I get it. Like, bright yellow.

00:12:21.807 --> 00:12:25.611
But Claudia, what you can't tell

00:12:25.611 --> 00:12:26.912
is how good this tastes.

00:12:29.115 --> 00:12:32.952
Other US sides you can get here: coleslaw.

00:12:32.952 --> 00:12:34.754
Claudia was talking about corn on the cob.

00:12:34.754 --> 00:12:38.390
We got corn off the cob, aka sweet corn.

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:41.260
I'm just thinking, in terms
of the American experience,

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:44.897
I don't want to be all,
like, doing this at my desk

00:12:44.897 --> 00:12:46.332
when I get KFC for lunch, you know?

00:12:46.332 --> 00:12:48.067
I just want to eat it and get going, so.

00:12:48.067 --> 00:12:50.369
Another thing we have here, biscuits.

00:12:50.369 --> 00:12:52.438
And I feel like you get these
with these types of meals

00:12:52.438 --> 00:12:53.973
because it's good at sopping up things,

00:12:53.973 --> 00:12:55.908
like good at sopping up the gravy.

00:12:55.908 --> 00:12:58.778
On their own, they're
just so ... [thudding].

00:12:58.778 --> 00:13:01.113
I want to see if I can eat
one without any liquid,

00:13:01.113 --> 00:13:03.149
like, how long it takes me
to eat a dry one. Ready?

00:13:03.149 --> 00:13:05.584
This is how dry these
are. Ready? Time me. Go.

00:13:11.123 --> 00:13:12.424
Only halfway through!

00:13:18.998 --> 00:13:21.333
Ugh, it hurts to talk.

00:13:21.333 --> 00:13:22.434
Time.

00:13:23.602 --> 00:13:24.904
Yeah, not my favorite.

00:13:24.904 --> 00:13:26.839
Another exclusive you
can get here in the US

00:13:26.839 --> 00:13:28.941
is a piece of à la carte chicken.

00:13:28.941 --> 00:13:31.744
I feel like if you went into
a KFC in Italy and was like,

00:13:31.744 --> 00:13:33.546
"I just want one drumstick,"
they'd give it to you.

00:13:33.546 --> 00:13:35.281
I don't think they'd
really push back on it.

00:13:35.281 --> 00:13:36.849
But our menu specifically has,

00:13:36.849 --> 00:13:38.818
you get an individual piece of chicken.

00:13:38.818 --> 00:13:40.986
You can get a drumstick,
a thigh, or a breast.

00:13:40.986 --> 00:13:44.623
You get chicken in this hand,
Famous Bowl in this hand,

00:13:44.623 --> 00:13:46.492
and walk right into traffic.

00:13:46.492 --> 00:13:48.360
Sauce talk, let's go.

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:50.429
Discorso di la salsa.

00:13:50.429 --> 00:13:52.531
In Italy, we have some exclusive sauces,

00:13:52.531 --> 00:13:54.600
starting from the original.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:57.603
I know you guys in the
US have the KFC sauce.

00:13:57.603 --> 00:13:59.738
Does this look similar?

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:04.410
I think if I were making sauces,
I would've just continued,

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:07.112
you know, trialing others after this one.

00:14:09.148 --> 00:14:11.584
Yeah, it's, like, a
mayo-y barbecue ketchup.

00:14:11.584 --> 00:14:14.920
And then we have the smoky barbecue sauce.

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:17.556
And then we have the sweet imperial sauce.

00:14:17.556 --> 00:14:20.826
That's a sweet and sour sauce.

00:14:20.826 --> 00:14:23.495
Very lemony, but fresh.

00:14:23.495 --> 00:14:24.830
Yeah, it's a nice one. I like this.

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:28.634
Then move on to the 2 hot 4 U.

00:14:28.634 --> 00:14:29.902
Jelly-like.

00:14:30.836 --> 00:14:33.405
It's not too hot for you,
it's just too bad for me.

00:14:33.405 --> 00:14:36.008
Moving on, we also have garlic sauce.

00:14:36.008 --> 00:14:37.877
I know you guys associate Italy

00:14:37.877 --> 00:14:39.712
and Italian cuisine with garlic.

00:14:39.712 --> 00:14:41.480
Please stop doing that.

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:43.549
We don't really like it.

00:14:43.549 --> 00:14:45.985
Then we have a fresh pepper one.

00:14:45.985 --> 00:14:48.053
This one apparently contains cheese.

00:14:48.954 --> 00:14:50.389
Tastes like not much, to be honest.

00:14:50.389 --> 00:14:52.458
We also have creamy curry.

00:14:52.458 --> 00:14:55.427
Finally, we couldn't
get the only olive oil,

00:14:55.427 --> 00:14:58.063
but we do have olive oil and white vinegar

00:14:58.063 --> 00:15:01.333
and olive oil and balsamic vinegar.

00:15:01.333 --> 00:15:04.837
I don't know if you want to
consider olive oil a sauce.

00:15:04.837 --> 00:15:06.572
I have mixed feeling about it,

00:15:06.572 --> 00:15:08.707
because that's definitely more dressing.

00:15:08.707 --> 00:15:11.944
Are you curious to see how
chicken olive oil tastes like?

00:15:11.944 --> 00:15:12.945
Let's try it.

00:15:12.945 --> 00:15:16.048
Olive oil and balsamic vinegar. Let's see.

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:19.418
Kind of brought it back
to life a little bit,

00:15:19.418 --> 00:15:21.320
because it had cooled down.

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:22.855
Yeah, I should do this
more often, actually.

00:15:22.855 --> 00:15:25.958
It tastes less fried for some reason.

00:15:25.958 --> 00:15:27.626
Because I always associate olive oil

00:15:27.626 --> 00:15:28.961
with, like, grilled chicken.

00:15:28.961 --> 00:15:31.764
So if you want to trick
your mind into thinking

00:15:31.764 --> 00:15:34.266
that you're eating grilled
chicken and not fried,

00:15:34.266 --> 00:15:37.603
maybe all you have to do is
pour some olive oil on it.

00:15:37.603 --> 00:15:38.570
Joe: Honey mustard.

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:41.106
Honey barbecue.

00:15:42.141 --> 00:15:43.842
That's good. Buffalo ranch.

00:15:43.842 --> 00:15:46.312
If you are unaware, we have a sauce here

00:15:46.312 --> 00:15:48.314
that usually is on wings
called the Buffalo sauce.

00:15:48.314 --> 00:15:50.783
It's a vinegary hot sauce

00:15:50.783 --> 00:15:54.420
that is a little north of mild.

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:56.755
And the reason that
Buffalo ranch is a thing

00:15:56.755 --> 00:15:59.758
is because when you eat Buffalo
wings and they're spicy,

00:15:59.758 --> 00:16:04.596
you dip the wings in ranch, a
second sauce, to cool it down.

00:16:04.596 --> 00:16:05.998
So we as Americans are used

00:16:05.998 --> 00:16:08.167
to pairing Buffalo sauce on the wings

00:16:08.167 --> 00:16:09.435
with ranch dressing.

00:16:09.435 --> 00:16:11.270
So they were like, let's
just put it in one,

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:13.772
because God forbid we have two sauces.

00:16:13.772 --> 00:16:15.174
But if you want to have
just regular ranch,

00:16:15.174 --> 00:16:16.942
everyone on the internet
come at me, all right?

00:16:16.942 --> 00:16:19.678
Ranch is just OK. It all tastes the same.

00:16:19.678 --> 00:16:20.913
Also we have a hot sauce.

00:16:20.913 --> 00:16:22.014
A honey sauce.

00:16:22.014 --> 00:16:24.516
We have a lot of dessert
options here in Italy.

00:16:24.516 --> 00:16:26.986
Most of them are just ice cream.

00:16:26.986 --> 00:16:29.588
We start from a plain ice cream cone.

00:16:29.588 --> 00:16:31.156
Then you can get sundaes.

00:16:31.156 --> 00:16:33.225
They come plain, caramel flavor,

00:16:33.225 --> 00:16:35.527
Nutella, strawberry, and chocolate.

00:16:35.527 --> 00:16:37.496
And then we have these, the Kream Balls.

00:16:37.496 --> 00:16:40.599
They come with Nutella flavor, caramel,

00:16:40.599 --> 00:16:42.568
strawberry, and chocolate.

00:16:42.568 --> 00:16:44.370
They're kind of similar to a sundae,

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:47.406
but they have this crunchy bottom.

00:16:47.406 --> 00:16:48.974
And apparently the caramel one

00:16:48.974 --> 00:16:50.542
is supposed to have lots of layers.

00:16:50.542 --> 00:16:51.577
This is the caramel one.

00:16:51.577 --> 00:16:54.780
But I'm not sure we can
judge the number of layers,

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:57.016
because it has absolutely melted.

00:16:57.016 --> 00:17:01.086
So, we got a Nutella Kream
Ball and a caramel one.

00:17:01.086 --> 00:17:03.856
You know those backpacks for cats?

00:17:03.856 --> 00:17:06.692
I think it's the same thing here.

00:17:06.692 --> 00:17:09.061
I'm curious about the crunchy bottom.

00:17:09.061 --> 00:17:11.096
Oh, yeah, that is crunchy.

00:17:13.399 --> 00:17:15.634
Actually it reminds me a little bit of

00:17:15.634 --> 00:17:17.736
the Algida, the Cornetto.

00:17:17.736 --> 00:17:20.239
It may have another name in the US.

00:17:20.239 --> 00:17:23.575
And they have that
crunchy bit at the bottom.

00:17:23.575 --> 00:17:26.979
I mean, for us Italian, Nutella
is like the OG chocolate.

00:17:26.979 --> 00:17:29.715
Before chocolate always comes Nutella,

00:17:29.715 --> 00:17:31.417
just no questions asked.

00:17:31.417 --> 00:17:34.053
It's always been like this.
And before cream as well.

00:17:34.053 --> 00:17:37.056
The only exclusive dessert
option we have in America

00:17:37.056 --> 00:17:39.091
is this: a chocolate cake.

00:17:39.091 --> 00:17:40.225
And it just occurred to me,

00:17:40.225 --> 00:17:42.061
I've actually never had this cake.

00:17:42.061 --> 00:17:43.662
Let's see how we did.

00:17:46.165 --> 00:17:47.499
Perfect.

00:17:47.499 --> 00:17:49.068
Cooked beautifully.

00:17:49.068 --> 00:17:52.371
It's got the right amount
of bounce, isn't dried out.

00:17:52.371 --> 00:17:53.672
And now we taste it.

00:17:57.142 --> 00:17:58.677
Exquisite.

00:17:58.677 --> 00:18:01.413
You keep baking like that,
you can win this competition.

00:18:01.413 --> 00:18:03.282
I started off as Gordon Ramsay.

00:18:03.282 --> 00:18:05.617
Every impression I do of
anyone is just kind of that.

00:18:05.617 --> 00:18:06.685
This is actually pretty good.

00:18:06.685 --> 00:18:10.122
Yeah, they had those
balls, those Kream Balls,

00:18:10.122 --> 00:18:12.558
which is kind of a weird thing to call it.

00:18:12.558 --> 00:18:14.259
No, I don't want any of those.

00:18:14.259 --> 00:18:16.495
I get it. I like dessert
just as much as the next guy.

00:18:16.495 --> 00:18:19.598
But KFC, I want to load
up on fried chicken.

00:18:19.598 --> 00:18:21.400
I want to load up on mac and cheese.

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:23.102
I want to load up on mashed potatoes.

00:18:23.102 --> 00:18:24.570
I want to load up on corn.

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:27.139
If only someone could put
it all in one bowl for me.

00:18:27.139 --> 00:18:29.174
Dessert? No, I want to eat fried chicken

00:18:29.174 --> 00:18:31.410
until I'm about to burst,
and then I'm out. So.

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:33.245
The exclusive drinks in Italy are

00:18:33.245 --> 00:18:36.648
7Up, Lipton iced tea, and beer.

00:18:36.648 --> 00:18:38.350
Fountain drinks you can get in the US.

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:39.518
We do have a bunch of exclusives.

00:18:39.518 --> 00:18:41.553
I didn't get every single one, relax.

00:18:41.553 --> 00:18:43.088
All right, starting down here.

00:18:43.088 --> 00:18:44.556
Sweet tea.

00:18:44.556 --> 00:18:46.125
Oh, yeah, their lemonade.

00:18:46.125 --> 00:18:47.092
It's really good. It's addictive.

00:18:47.092 --> 00:18:51.130
And our lemonade is not
carbonated, it's still.

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:52.598
Mountain Dew, it's fantastic.

00:18:52.598 --> 00:18:54.299
And the reason I saved this one for last,

00:18:54.299 --> 00:18:59.004
it's something you can get
exclusively at the KFC in the US,

00:18:59.004 --> 00:19:01.206
it's Mountain Dew Sweet Lightning.

00:19:01.206 --> 00:19:03.375
It's so good. Like, you
just know it's super sweet,

00:19:03.375 --> 00:19:05.277
and super chemically, but I love it.

00:19:05.277 --> 00:19:08.313
Other drinks you can get at
a US KFC that we did not get

00:19:08.313 --> 00:19:11.049
was Starry and blackberry lemonade,

00:19:11.049 --> 00:19:12.484
which is currently unavailable.

00:19:14.086 --> 00:19:16.722
Which country's getting
a better deal on its KFC?

00:19:16.722 --> 00:19:19.191
Let's compare a few
menu items to find out.

00:19:19.191 --> 00:19:21.894
Looking at the chicken
sandwich combo meal,

00:19:21.894 --> 00:19:23.829
which comes with a side
and a medium drink,

00:19:23.829 --> 00:19:27.432
this whole thing in Los
Angeles would cost you $10.99.

00:19:27.432 --> 00:19:30.969
Note, if you got each item
individually, added up,

00:19:30.969 --> 00:19:33.338
it would be $12.77.

00:19:33.338 --> 00:19:36.008
In Italy, you can also get a similar meal

00:19:36.008 --> 00:19:37.809
that is called a Zinger meal,

00:19:37.809 --> 00:19:39.545
and that includes a sandwich,

00:19:39.545 --> 00:19:41.480
a side of choice, and a drink.

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:43.815
This will cost you 10 euros and 40 cents.

00:19:43.815 --> 00:19:48.187
At the time of recording,
that is equal to $11.52.

00:19:48.187 --> 00:19:52.090
So that is 5% more
expensive than the US meal.

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:54.259
If you order these items individually,

00:19:54.259 --> 00:19:56.962
that will cost you 13 euros and 60 cents,

00:19:56.962 --> 00:19:59.898
and that's about $15.06.

00:19:59.898 --> 00:20:02.868
We also took a look at
KFC's most expensive items.

00:20:02.868 --> 00:20:05.437
In Italy, the most
expensive item on the menu

00:20:05.437 --> 00:20:07.472
is the 16-piece bucket.

00:20:07.472 --> 00:20:10.542
This one costs 42 euros 90 cents,

00:20:10.542 --> 00:20:14.179
which is about $47.51.

00:20:14.179 --> 00:20:16.014
This is supposed to feed four people

00:20:16.014 --> 00:20:19.318
for $11.87 per person.

00:20:19.318 --> 00:20:21.320
The most expensive item on the US menu

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:23.288
is the 16-piece chicken meal,

00:20:23.288 --> 00:20:25.624
which includes 16 pieces of chicken,

00:20:25.624 --> 00:20:26.925
original or crispy,

00:20:26.925 --> 00:20:28.860
four large sides, eight biscuits,

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:32.464
and it costs you $52.99.

00:20:32.464 --> 00:20:35.067
Now, this is meant to feed
seven to eight people.

00:20:35.067 --> 00:20:35.901
Sure.

00:20:35.901 --> 00:20:39.238
And it costs roughly $6.62 per person,

00:20:39.238 --> 00:20:42.975
which is 44% cheaper than
Italy's per-person cost.

00:20:42.975 --> 00:20:45.744
Italy KFC puts a lot of effort

00:20:45.744 --> 00:20:48.180
into its meals and special offers

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:50.449
so they can be a better
value for the money.

00:20:50.449 --> 00:20:54.319
Personally, in Italy, we're not
really used to having meals.

00:20:54.319 --> 00:20:58.624
We are very accustomed to
just having a big main course.

00:20:58.624 --> 00:21:01.627
That to me still feels a
bit of an American thing.

00:21:01.627 --> 00:21:03.328
But this is American food,

00:21:03.328 --> 00:21:06.298
so I guess we are using
their customs as well.

00:21:06.298 --> 00:21:07.866
If you're operating under the assumption

00:21:07.866 --> 00:21:10.636
that this is for seven people,
it's a pretty good deal.

00:21:10.636 --> 00:21:14.072
But you and I both know
this ain't for seven people.

00:21:15.807 --> 00:21:18.010
We want to see if there
are any similarities

00:21:18.010 --> 00:21:21.246
in the nutrition of
KFC for both countries.

00:21:21.246 --> 00:21:22.381
Now, this is our chicken sandwich,

00:21:22.381 --> 00:21:25.550
and it has 650 calories.

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:26.618
And if you'll notice,

00:21:26.618 --> 00:21:28.387
there's a lot of salt
and fat in this sandwich,

00:21:28.387 --> 00:21:31.023
over half your daily recommended intake.

00:21:31.023 --> 00:21:33.258
KFC Italy doesn't disclose their calories

00:21:33.258 --> 00:21:34.393
on their website.

00:21:34.393 --> 00:21:37.029
Actually, I think disclosing
nutritional information,

00:21:37.029 --> 00:21:38.463
like calories and everything,

00:21:38.463 --> 00:21:40.732
I find that quite an American thing.

00:21:40.732 --> 00:21:42.334
That doesn't mean it's good or bad.

00:21:42.334 --> 00:21:43.935
It's just like, we don't really

00:21:43.935 --> 00:21:46.271
tend to count calories in things.

00:21:46.271 --> 00:21:49.308
Every "Food Wars" we've
done, all the nutrition info,

00:21:49.308 --> 00:21:51.143
all the ingredients info, in the US,

00:21:51.143 --> 00:21:52.878
you can get it, no problem.

00:21:52.878 --> 00:21:55.247
Other countries, they don't provide it.

00:21:57.049 --> 00:21:58.817
Let's take a look at some ingredients

00:21:58.817 --> 00:22:00.719
that KFC uses here in Italy.

00:22:00.719 --> 00:22:03.789
Here are all the
ingredients for the fries.

00:22:03.789 --> 00:22:05.657
Nine is a lot.

00:22:05.657 --> 00:22:08.126
Potatoes and frying oil, how about two?

00:22:08.126 --> 00:22:11.797
Two ingredients, and a bit
of salt, and one chemical.

00:22:11.797 --> 00:22:14.666
Let's just use one, you
know, if we have to.

00:22:14.666 --> 00:22:18.403
And here are all the ingredients
of the fries in the US.

00:22:18.403 --> 00:22:20.405
33 ingredients.

00:22:20.405 --> 00:22:23.942
That's 24 more than the
ingredients in Italy's fries.

00:22:23.942 --> 00:22:25.177
That's nuts.

00:22:25.177 --> 00:22:26.878
Claudia: Nine ingredients for this thing,

00:22:26.878 --> 00:22:28.780
and it doesn't even hold its shape.

00:22:28.780 --> 00:22:31.283
I would expect it to be perfect.

00:22:31.283 --> 00:22:33.452
There's a lot of flavors
and colorings that we use,

00:22:33.452 --> 00:22:36.254
like paprika, turmeric,
and annatto extract color,

00:22:36.254 --> 00:22:38.156
which is funny we put that into the fries,

00:22:38.156 --> 00:22:41.059
but when making this, KFC also
uses bleached white flour,

00:22:41.059 --> 00:22:42.694
which removes all the color,

00:22:42.694 --> 00:22:43.929
so it seems kind of counterproductive.

00:22:43.929 --> 00:22:45.297
Like, they're taking all the color out

00:22:45.297 --> 00:22:46.832
with the bleached flour, right?

00:22:46.832 --> 00:22:48.333
And they're putting all
those chemicals back in

00:22:48.333 --> 00:22:50.335
to make them look like fries.

00:22:50.335 --> 00:22:51.670
I don't know why we do that either.

00:22:51.670 --> 00:22:53.672
So, let's have a look at the ingredients

00:22:53.672 --> 00:22:55.741
for a chicken drumstick.

00:22:55.741 --> 00:22:58.744
Italy's chicken uses a
lot of flavor enhancers,

00:22:58.744 --> 00:23:00.712
gums, and stabilizers.

00:23:00.712 --> 00:23:03.648
For example, xanthan gum and guar gum.

00:23:03.648 --> 00:23:05.317
They're used in meat products

00:23:05.317 --> 00:23:08.320
to keep the chicken tender
during the cooking process.

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:10.756
These gums are also used for chicken

00:23:10.756 --> 00:23:14.192
that has a batter around
it, so that when it's fried,

00:23:14.192 --> 00:23:15.961
it absorbs less oil.

00:23:15.961 --> 00:23:18.830
As I said before, Italians
don't really look at ingredients

00:23:18.830 --> 00:23:21.199
or nutritional value of things.

00:23:21.199 --> 00:23:22.334
And that is why I think there is

00:23:22.334 --> 00:23:25.704
a lot of work done beforehand for us

00:23:25.704 --> 00:23:27.906
in order to make the food
as simple as possible,

00:23:27.906 --> 00:23:29.808
so that if you do look at the ingredients,

00:23:29.808 --> 00:23:32.110
you are not so shocked by it.

00:23:32.110 --> 00:23:35.580
And here are the ingredients
of the chicken in the US.

00:23:35.580 --> 00:23:37.282
Surprisingly smaller than Italy's list,

00:23:37.282 --> 00:23:40.218
although the US has not noted
what oil they use for frying,

00:23:40.218 --> 00:23:41.420
like Italy has.

00:23:41.420 --> 00:23:44.256
So it would probably add
a few more ingredients.

00:23:44.256 --> 00:23:46.658
Now, KFC actually uses pressure frying

00:23:46.658 --> 00:23:48.827
instead of deep frying,
like the other chains,

00:23:48.827 --> 00:23:50.929
as it allows for faster cooking time

00:23:50.929 --> 00:23:52.798
and always keeps the meat moister,

00:23:52.798 --> 00:23:54.299
as less steam evaporates.

00:23:54.299 --> 00:23:56.468
Let's take a closer look
at a few ingredients

00:23:56.468 --> 00:23:58.370
that some of us may not recognize.

00:23:58.370 --> 00:24:01.206
OK, first up, sodium phosphate.

00:24:01.206 --> 00:24:03.542
Now, it helps stabilize the pH of the food

00:24:03.542 --> 00:24:04.943
to keep them together.

00:24:04.943 --> 00:24:07.746
But it's also popular
over-the-counter medicine

00:24:07.746 --> 00:24:09.581
for bowel movements.

00:24:09.581 --> 00:24:11.316
So don't be surprised if eating KFC

00:24:11.316 --> 00:24:14.152
makes you rush to the bathroom.

00:24:14.152 --> 00:24:17.823
Next up, monosodium glutamate,

00:24:17.823 --> 00:24:21.092
flavor enhancer commonly added
to soups and processed meats.

00:24:21.092 --> 00:24:23.462
Ugh. We're putting these
names on-screen, right?

00:24:23.462 --> 00:24:26.631
Ah, this word looks like this

00:24:26.631 --> 00:24:28.633
and is probably pronounced

00:24:28.633 --> 00:24:32.571
dime-thigh-polo-sigh-lexane.

00:24:32.571 --> 00:24:34.606
Computer: Dimethylpolysiloxane.

00:24:34.606 --> 00:24:37.175
It's an antifoaming agent
derived from silicone,

00:24:37.175 --> 00:24:40.479
usually added to oils,
jams, and canned vegetables.

00:24:40.479 --> 00:24:43.315
Disodium dihydrogen pyrophosphate.

00:24:43.315 --> 00:24:45.150
This should be a contest. Anyway. OK.

00:24:45.150 --> 00:24:47.652
Prevents potatoes in the
fries from turning brown

00:24:47.652 --> 00:24:49.488
due to oxidization,

00:24:49.488 --> 00:24:52.224
which is natural for most
fruits and vegetables.

00:24:52.224 --> 00:24:53.825
And just to add that all these ingredients

00:24:53.825 --> 00:24:55.660
have been approved by health professionals

00:24:55.660 --> 00:24:57.529
and there are no safety concerns,

00:24:57.529 --> 00:25:00.532
as long as they're eaten
in lower quantities,

00:25:00.532 --> 00:25:03.401
which, in general, is good
advice for eating fast food.

00:25:03.401 --> 00:25:06.738
Chickens in the US are free of
added hormones and steroids.

00:25:06.738 --> 00:25:09.207
However, KFC does not disclose much else

00:25:09.207 --> 00:25:10.909
about how the chicken is prepared,

00:25:10.909 --> 00:25:13.745
nor how much chicken is used per item.

00:25:13.745 --> 00:25:17.182
As of 2019, Yum Brands,
the parent company of KFC,

00:25:17.182 --> 00:25:20.585
stopped purchasing chicken
raised using antibiotics.

00:25:20.585 --> 00:25:22.854
So I guess they're heading
in the right direction.

00:25:24.823 --> 00:25:28.627
KFC opened their first outlet in the '70s

00:25:28.627 --> 00:25:30.629
in Naples for some reason.

00:25:30.629 --> 00:25:32.964
And then that didn't work
out, and they closed.

00:25:32.964 --> 00:25:35.567
And then they came back to Italy in 2014.

00:25:35.567 --> 00:25:39.638
The objective was to open
100 branches in four years.

00:25:39.638 --> 00:25:41.273
They're not quite there yet.

00:25:41.273 --> 00:25:43.174
As of 2022, the stats say

00:25:43.174 --> 00:25:46.645
that they've opened 68
branches here in Italy.

00:25:46.645 --> 00:25:48.346
Although it's been here since 2014,

00:25:48.346 --> 00:25:50.582
it does still feel pretty new.

00:25:50.582 --> 00:25:53.485
Like, Italians are not so big on chicken,

00:25:53.485 --> 00:25:54.853
especially grilled chicken.

00:25:54.853 --> 00:25:58.657
It does still feel like
a very foreign idea.

00:25:58.657 --> 00:26:01.293
KFC is so popular in the US,

00:26:01.293 --> 00:26:03.528
maybe the most popular chicken chain,

00:26:03.528 --> 00:26:04.729
fried-chicken chain at least.

00:26:04.729 --> 00:26:06.865
I think it's the

00:26:06.865 --> 00:26:10.502
fried-chicken chain to beat in the US.

00:26:10.502 --> 00:26:12.904
There's other chicken places
that do chicken sandwiches,

00:26:12.904 --> 00:26:15.807
chicken burgers. But as
far as chicken on the bone,

00:26:15.807 --> 00:26:17.876
I don't know who's even
competing with KFC.

00:26:17.876 --> 00:26:19.644
Ah, I guess there's Popeyes.

00:26:19.644 --> 00:26:20.912
Oh, yeah, Popeyes.

00:26:20.912 --> 00:26:23.248
No, I think KFC is way
more popular than Popeyes.

00:26:23.248 --> 00:26:24.583
I didn't say it's better.

00:26:24.583 --> 00:26:27.319
If a KFC opens in a new town,

00:26:27.319 --> 00:26:29.721
for example, in my hometown
they opened last year,

00:26:29.721 --> 00:26:31.289
there are huge lines.

00:26:31.289 --> 00:26:33.124
There are a lot of people
that want to try it

00:26:33.124 --> 00:26:34.426
because it's really the idea

00:26:34.426 --> 00:26:37.028
of the American fast-food
chain that's arriving.

00:26:37.028 --> 00:26:39.097
So it's exciting. It's different.

00:26:39.097 --> 00:26:40.632
Again, it's one of those
things that I think

00:26:40.632 --> 00:26:42.701
you do try it because of the hype.

00:26:42.701 --> 00:26:45.837
KFC adaptability is
weird. A couple years ago,

00:26:45.837 --> 00:26:47.672
there used to be a lot
more stuff on the menu.

00:26:47.672 --> 00:26:49.107
And now there's a lot less.

00:26:49.107 --> 00:26:51.876
So their adaptability is
less about making stuff

00:26:51.876 --> 00:26:54.079
that kind of caters to people's tastes,

00:26:54.079 --> 00:26:56.514
and more like, "No
one's getting the wings,

00:26:56.514 --> 00:26:57.949
let's just do the nuggets.

00:26:57.949 --> 00:26:59.718
Let's take all this stuff off the menu,

00:26:59.718 --> 00:27:01.987
let's pare it down, go,
go, go," for efficiency,

00:27:01.987 --> 00:27:04.389
and probably because it's
cheaper to have less ingredients.

00:27:04.389 --> 00:27:08.226
So they've adapted to, I don't know,

00:27:08.226 --> 00:27:11.029
shifts in the market or
people's interest in KFC.

00:27:11.029 --> 00:27:13.865
They really don't deviate
too far, dish-wise,

00:27:13.865 --> 00:27:17.969
from, like, a fried chicken
or a chicken in a bun.

00:27:17.969 --> 00:27:20.438
KFC is actually the chain that has made

00:27:20.438 --> 00:27:23.308
the least effort to Italianize the menu.

00:27:23.308 --> 00:27:24.743
I don't know. Actually, weirdly,

00:27:24.743 --> 00:27:26.845
I think that for this it works,

00:27:26.845 --> 00:27:29.114
because the idea of eating fried chicken

00:27:29.114 --> 00:27:31.950
is so foreign to us that I
don't know how you would,

00:27:31.950 --> 00:27:33.551
how would you make that Italian?

00:27:33.551 --> 00:27:35.053
You'd maybe put some, like,

00:27:35.053 --> 00:27:37.956
fried courgette flowers with the chicken?

00:27:37.956 --> 00:27:38.957
I don't know.

00:27:38.957 --> 00:27:42.160
For me to even think about
a similar Italian thing,

00:27:42.160 --> 00:27:46.131
that, weirdly, I think this
may be working the way it is.

00:27:46.131 --> 00:27:49.701
So we'll see when they
will reach 100 branches.

00:27:49.701 --> 00:27:51.369
Maybe sooner than we think.

00:27:51.369 --> 00:27:54.906
Make note of the fun Colonel
Sanders doing a cartwheel.

00:27:54.906 --> 00:27:56.841
Wasn't this guy, like, 70

00:27:56.841 --> 00:27:58.943
when he started Kentucky Fried Chicken?

00:27:58.943 --> 00:27:59.878
There's no way.

00:27:59.878 --> 00:28:02.580
If he's doing that, it's against his will.

00:28:04.649 --> 00:28:06.217
Moments before the ambulance was called.

